    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.27.6</title>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:00:19 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22706</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.27.6</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>One glyph for work in progress, everywhere: a small stream of pixels flowing like water, never repeating, so each working chat looks a little different. It moves only while something is actually working, and holds still under Reduce Motion.</li><li>Every other state is a still mark: an amber dot when a chat waits on you (no counts; the number is in the tooltip), a crossed circle when it failed, a yellow dot for unread. The wave-lines glyph and the 3×3 loader are gone.</li><li>An open pond no longer shows its status mark beside its name: its chats show their own.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.27.5</h4><ul><li>A queued message has its own Steer button on its line: one click sends it into the running turn. Clicking the line still opens the whole message to edit or remove it.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.27.4</h4><ul><li>The chat no longer jumps, flickers or shows a message twice while it updates. Every message has exactly one row from the moment you press Send: a message you send while Claude works is its queued line at once (no card above the composer that later moves into the chat), a steer is a dimmed row at the end of the running turn that turns solid in the same place when the agent reads it, and the reply being written is the running turn's last row, the place the finished reply takes. A randomized test races the host's events, the queue and your presses in 600 orders and fails on any duplicate, reordered, vanished or reappearing row.</li><li>A queued message is one short line in the chat (its first words, how many pictures, "Queued"). Click it to see the whole message and Steer, Edit or Remove it. Editing changes the words and keeps the pictures.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
